🧱 Phase 5 — Prompt Wrapping (Level 4)

👉 Purpose:

Control how input is given to the model

What it does:
Wraps user input
Adds system rules
Prevents instruction override
Protects against:
Role override
Direct prompt injection
Some multi-step attacks

🔒 Phase 6 — Output Filtering Level 5

👉 Purpose:

Control what comes OUT of the model

What it does:
Scans model response
Blocks sensitive info
Prevents leakage
Protects against:
Reflection attacks
Indirect extraction
Semantic leakage (what you observed)

🧠 Real-World Analogy

Think like this:

Prompt Wrapping = Security Guard at Entrance
Checks what goes inside
Output Filtering = Security Guard at Exit
Checks what goes outside

👉 You currently only have entrance security

